{"title":"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At each of the sixteen circles in the network below stands a student. A total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/82072a50d745a1ae7a12d81f37de0226f1028ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3360$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> coins are distributed among the sixteen students. All at once, all students give away all their coins by passing an equal number of coins to each of their neighbors in the network. After the trade, all students have the same number of coins as they started with. Find the number of coins the student standing at the center circle had originally.\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/a/33abde80848746d240bfc392b8997b80cf3bccd5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import cse5; unitsize(6mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); dotfactor = 8; pathpen=black;  pair A = (0,0); pair B = 2*dir(54), C = 2*dir(126), D = 2*dir(198), E = 2*dir(270), F = 2*dir(342); pair G = 3.6*dir(18), H = 3.6*dir(90), I = 3.6*dir(162), J = 3.6*dir(234), K = 3.6*dir(306); pair M = 6.4*dir(54), N = 6.4*dir(126), O = 6.4*dir(198), P = 6.4*dir(270), L = 6.4*dir(342); pair[] dotted = {A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J,K,L,M,N,O,P};  D(A--B--H--M); D(A--C--H--N); D(A--F--G--L); D(A--E--K--P); D(A--D--J--O); D(B--G--M); D(F--K--L); D(E--J--P); D(O--I--D); D(C--I--N); D(L--M--N--O--P--L);  dot(dotted);  [/asy]\" width=\"358\" height=\"342\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Say the student in the center starts out with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> coins, the students neighboring the center student each start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> coins, and all other students start out with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> coins. Then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />-coin student has five neighbors, all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />-coin students have three neighbors, and all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />-coin students have four neighbors.\n</p><p>Now in order for each student's number of coins to remain equal after the trade, the number of coins given by each student must be equal to the number received, and thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140a0297498a9fc895fafa81073005fbfc132170.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a &amp;= 5 \\cdot \\frac{b}{3}\\\\ b &amp;= \\frac{a}{5} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{c}{4}\\\\ c &amp;= 2 \\cdot \\frac{c}{4} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{b}{3}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"129\" height=\"121\" />\n</p><p>Solving these equations, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6ea122aeed8724a3432c08514e20c4d9d12b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a}{5} = \\frac{b}{3} = \\frac{c}{4}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"91\" height=\"38\" /> Also, the total number of coins is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d855e0992790941ed1415bc832444a3ba939beb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 5b + 10c = 3360,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/3/57387c06c3cfd2ec89531f456d5995db64fa8580.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 5 \\cdot \\frac{3a}{5} + 10 \\cdot \\frac{4a}{5} = 3360 \\rightarrow a = \\frac{3360}{12} = \\boxed{280}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"382\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>One way to make this more rigorous (answering the concern in Solution 3) is to let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> represent the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/f/c5fb123bf648cd63e59c43d10522d2d7cdbcb587.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$total$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> number of coins in the rings. Then, you don't care about individual people in the passing, you just know that each ring gets some coins and loses some coins, which must cancel each other out.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the students give the same number of gifts of coins as they receive and still end up the same number of coins, we can assume that every gift of coins has the same number of coins. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of coins in each gift of coins. There <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> people who give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gifts of coins, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people who give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gifts of coins, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> person who gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gifts of coins. Thus,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/a/9ba9c58befea95229a60899c688c281c38d4195d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 10(4x)+5(3x)+5x &amp;= 3360\\\\ 40x+15x+5x &amp;= 3360\\\\ 60x &amp;= 3360\\\\ x &amp;= 56 \\end{align*}\" width=\"216\" height=\"88\" />\nTherefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/d/7bdc070e6e0d5c33748fefabf438290be75aa288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5(56) = \\boxed{280}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mark the number of coins from inside to outside as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf4b756601df3422c1b49b0012b42d82119cc0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/6/af60415970796276254efa3327fce6c49f1e8414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/c/eac5694a43b35d28a1f4b889e52ada1cb9c2ce7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00322295674c54c5413520f7493470ff32ae3cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6d4142d351ef99cc26a94e44c1912d904dd4a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/a/94aaab012b431d7695fa1ae72d7a88b05baf09f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67cff48f601f12a5b71afe302e7c3487f7535731.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22dc9cbc8c15d4f632da82b3c13e496cd5358c5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/6/44612d9d6ec37da7f4edd0f205d65cdac5954dc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/7/117778db99ba8932dc35128d085c2619f4f690a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/0/aa004130b2df97e537d3b2a0e6f8affdd4a5403a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b5653fd5eb54c9c482049c473ec43f7df5b5d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb263569fd551843bdcef775ac67a1d053640f2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />.\nThen, we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f02215ade5023e1b167eeae2b83a507ea05fa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} d_1 &amp;= \\frac{d_5}{4} + \\frac{d_2}{4} + \\frac{c_1}{4} + \\frac{c_2}{4}\\\\ d_2 &amp;= \\frac{d_1}{4} + \\frac{d_3}{4} + \\frac{c_2}{4} + \\frac{c_3}{4}\\\\ d_3 &amp;= \\frac{d_2}{4} + \\frac{d_4}{4} + \\frac{c_3}{4} + \\frac{c_4}{4}\\\\ d_4 &amp;= \\frac{d_3}{4} + \\frac{d_5}{4} + \\frac{c_4}{4} + \\frac{c_5}{4}\\\\ d_5 &amp;= \\frac{d_4}{4} + \\frac{d_1}{4} + \\frac{c_5}{4} + \\frac{c_1}{4}\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"185\" height=\"213\" />\nLetting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e4225c741fd0f61b75a711097c0e9498a5d3a76e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = d_1 + d_2 + d_3 + d_4 + d_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"212\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/8/b98e1d94c5a0aada40d47b4c02704829d799f71a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = c_1 + c_2 + c_3 + c_4 + c_5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"202\" height=\"15\" /> gets us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/0/8d0dc4d4742f214fa2371881a2a4fceeaa9226e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = \\frac{D}{4} + \\frac{D}{4} + \\frac{C}{4} + \\frac{C}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/9/cc937808e48346cc1f8f735e2b5439609e4bf619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = C$\" width=\"54\" height=\"12\" />.\nIn the same way, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/e/63e50760c5a58ad8b310c7ea7afa0fcd339b748d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\frac{D}{4} + \\frac{D}{4} + \\frac{B}{3} + \\frac{B}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"183\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/0/d30bc7d84cccca0c2bba0c6aa7331cc45d63ff7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\frac{3D}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"66\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3957de5fda08bccad234323a3c50bc4b1cb473b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\frac{C}{4} + \\frac{C}{4} + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/209ccea8c0c5cb55a391604fb9ea1a045392c985.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{D}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />.\nThen, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/c/fec306f290b79c51b7b8065332f6eb871b91f8c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + B + C + D = 3360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"183\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4bade1fb0c8285fd7cd6abce15c3169da559ab0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D = 1120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"75\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e86bace1b36509f0438669ec6c6e82de56e8c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\boxed{280}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> as the number of coins the student in the middle has. Since this student connects to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other students, each of those students must have passed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54b5be3227874cd8745414c905d046797d9fa05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac15 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins to the center to maintain the same number of coins.\n</p><p>Each of these students connect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other students, passing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54b5be3227874cd8745414c905d046797d9fa05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac15 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins to each, so they must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fece360b4939e529bde4499ca79899bfd49919c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac35 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins. These students must then recieve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fece360b4939e529bde4499ca79899bfd49919c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac35 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3f6eb6d79b5751648caa9ebfd7ca26eade1569b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac 15 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> of which were given to by the center student. Thus, they must also have received \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa2ab266a4ba1ca903b324a0ab365255f595b43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac25 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> coins from the outer layer, and since this figure has symmetry, these must be the same.\n</p><p>Each of the next layer of students must have given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54b5be3227874cd8745414c905d046797d9fa05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac15 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins. Since they gave <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> people coins, they must have started with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae32539d719bf4d1a6bc123b1d43a1b084bc908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac45 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins. They received <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa2ab266a4ba1ca903b324a0ab365255f595b43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac25 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"25\" height=\"38\" /> of them from the inner layer, making the two other connections have given them the same amount. By a similar argument, they recieved <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54b5be3227874cd8745414c905d046797d9fa05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac15 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> from each of them.\n</p><p>By a similar argument, the outermost hexagon of students must have had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/e/cae32539d719bf4d1a6bc123b1d43a1b084bc908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac45 x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"23\" height=\"37\" /> coins each. Summing this all up, we get the number of total coins passed out as a function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. This ends up to be \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba25cdf6f1243f99fa8238defcdd1a4f59134945.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac45 x + \\dfrac35 x + \\dfrac35 x + \\dfrac35 x + \\dfrac35 x + \\dfrac35 x + x &amp;= 10 \\cdot \\dfrac45 x  + 5 \\cdot \\dfrac35 x + x \\\\  &amp;= 8x + 3x + x \\\\  &amp;= 12 x.  \\end{align*}\" width=\"873\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p>Since this all sums up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/82072a50d745a1ae7a12d81f37de0226f1028ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3360$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />, which is given, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b26b7a80ae3f280109da447c1f28f51050e20cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 12x &amp;= 3360 \\\\ x &amp;= 280 \\end{align*}\" width=\"86\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We defined <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to be the number of coins that the center person has, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3aba6584c68ab0c74b14e4a888795a179b2be549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{280}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012aimei/343\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012aimei/343</a>\n</p><p>~ dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I\" title=\"2012 AIME I\">2012 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017225517\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.073 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 462/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1786/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 108/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14860/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.188      1 -total\n 56.18%    7.409      1 Template:AIME_box\n 41.55%    5.480      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10867:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017225517 and revision id 205680. R